{"timestamp": 1779379992.650522, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 6, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779380009.939341, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Body is in electrical. I had just walked in from medbay and found Diana dead on the floor, so I reported it immediately. Charlie walked in right behind me just as I was hitting the button. I didn't see the killer leaving or anyone else around. Bob, you were in medbay with us just before this \u2014 did you see anyone heading toward electrical earlier?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779380018.274847, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I\u2019ve been in navigation the whole round and haven\u2019t seen anyone yet, so I can\u2019t confirm anything around electrical or medbay. I didn\u2019t see Diana at all. Eve\u2019s report makes sense location-wise, but I don\u2019t have info on who was near electrical. Bob and Charlie should say exactly where they came from and whether they saw anyone else around medbay/electrical."}}
{"timestamp": 1779380046.950016, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I started oxygen, went through upper engine, then into medbay. In medbay I saw Charlie there around ticks 4 and 5. I also saw Eve leave medbay toward electrical at tick 4. I never saw Diana at all, and I didn\u2019t see anyone else pass through medbay.\n\nSo from my view, Charlie was still in medbay after Eve had already gone toward electrical, which makes Eve getting there first line up. Charlie could\u2019ve followed after tick 5, but I don\u2019t think Charlie was right behind Eve the whole time. Eve had the earliest access to electrical from what I saw, but she did report, so I\u2019m not hard accusing yet. Need to hear Charlie and Frank\u2019s routes."}}
{"timestamp": 1779380067.122858, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I started cafeteria and went to medbay. In medbay I saw Eve there early, and Frank was also in medbay around tick 2. Eve was still in medbay at tick 3, then I saw Eve leave medbay toward electrical at tick 4. Bob entered medbay from upper engine at about the same time, and I saw Bob in medbay after that.\n\nI followed toward electrical after Eve, but I was not on top of her the whole time \u2014 Bob is right that I was still in medbay briefly after Eve left. When I got into electrical, Eve was reporting Diana\u2019s body. I did not see Diana alive at all, and I didn\u2019t see anyone else leaving electrical.\n\nSo from my view: Eve had first access to electrical from medbay and reported the body, which could be innocent or a self-report. Bob\u2019s medbay story matches what I saw. The big missing piece is Frank \u2014 I saw Frank in medbay early, then lost track of him, and he could potentially have gone toward electrical before Eve. I want Frank\u2019s exact route before we decide."}}
{"timestamp": 1779380086.901972, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I started in electrical and went out to medbay pretty early. I did not see Diana or any body in electrical when I was there. At about tick 2 I was in medbay and saw both Eve and Charlie there. After that I moved up to upper engine, so I wasn\u2019t near electrical when the report happened.\n\nBob and Charlie\u2019s stories line up with what I saw in medbay. If Eve left medbay toward electrical first and then immediately reported Diana there, that makes Eve the main person with access after I left, unless Alice is lying about being in navigation the whole time and came through security. I don\u2019t have a hard accusation, but from the accounts, Eve is the most suspicious because she found the body in the room she went to alone."}}
{"timestamp": 1779380110.5999858, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Frank, your logic makes sense on paper, but think about the reality of the situation. I knew Charlie was trailing right behind me from medbay. If I just killed Diana, why would I immediately self-report the exact second Charlie walks in? That would be an incredibly sloppy and risky play. I hit the button because I walked in, found her dead, and knew Charlie was right there \u2014 I wasn't going to just walk away and let him think I did it.\n\nAlso, notice that absolutely no one saw Diana all game. She wasn't in medbay with the rest of us, and Alice claims she didn't see her near navigation. She most likely came from the right side of the map, like security or storage. Frank, you started in electrical \u2014 is it possible you killed her right at the start before coming to medbay? Or Alice, is it possible you aren't being totally honest about seeing no one? \n\nI know I'm an easy target here because I reported it, but I promise you I didn't do it. Given we don't have a clear suspect, I really think we should skip rather than guessing and losing a Goose. I'm voting skip."}}
{"timestamp": 1779380135.0432231, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I still don\u2019t have any direct info from navigation \u2014 I saw nobody, no body, and no one came through my vision. So I can\u2019t clear or accuse anyone from my own sightings.\n\nFrom everyone\u2019s stories, Bob and Charlie seem to match each other pretty well in medbay. That leaves the suspicious window mostly between Eve and Frank. Eve did report, but she was also first into electrical from medbay. Frank starting in electrical is also important, because if Diana died early then Frank had the best opportunity before leaving.\n\nI don\u2019t think we have enough to be certain. I\u2019m most suspicious of Frank or Eve, but I\u2019d rather not force a bad vote unless someone has stronger timing. I\u2019m leaning skip for now, and we should watch Frank/Eve closely next round."}}
{"timestamp": 1779380154.161897, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "My info is still: oxygen -> upper engine -> medbay. I saw Charlie in medbay at ticks 4 and 5, and I saw Eve leave medbay toward electrical at tick 4. I never saw Diana at all, and I never saw Frank in upper engine or medbay from my own vision.\n\nCharlie\u2019s story matches mine pretty closely, so I feel better about Charlie. The main question is timing on Diana\u2019s death. If she was already dead in electrical before Eve arrived, then Frank starting in electrical is really important. If she died right as Eve got there, then Eve is suspicious, but reporting with Charlie close behind would be a risky self-report.\n\nI don\u2019t think there\u2019s enough certainty to vote someone out yet. I\u2019m most wary of Frank and Eve, but I\u2019m leaning skip unless someone has stronger timing."}}
{"timestamp": 1779380182.6285481, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I\u2019ll restate my timing because I think it matters: I was in medbay with Eve around ticks 2\u20133, then Bob came in from upper engine at tick 4 while Eve left toward electrical. I stayed in medbay briefly with Bob, then followed toward electrical after Eve. When I arrived, Eve was already reporting Diana\u2019s body. I never saw Diana alive, and I didn\u2019t see anyone leaving electrical.\n\nBob\u2019s story matches mine very closely, so I\u2019m feeling pretty good about Bob for now. Alice being in navigation gives no direct info either way.\n\nFor me the only realistic suspects from timing are Eve or Frank. Eve had first access from medbay and found the body, but a self-report with me coming in right behind her feels risky. Frank starting in electrical is also suspicious because if Diana died early, he had the cleanest chance before anyone else got there.\n\nI don\u2019t think we have enough certainty to eject. I\u2019m leaning skip, but next round we should keep a very close eye on Frank and Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779380195.328691, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 6, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I\u2019ll clarify my side again because I\u2019m getting named a lot: I did start in electrical, but I left very early and I did not see Diana there, dead or alive. By tick 2 I was already in medbay, where I saw both Eve and Charlie. After that I went up to upper engine, so I wasn\u2019t in electrical when Eve reported.\n\nThe timing matters: if Diana was already dead at the very start, then yes, I look possible because I started there. But if she died after I left, then it\u2019s much more likely someone came in after me. Bob and Charlie seem to confirm each other pretty strongly in medbay, and Eve reporting with Charlie close behind does make a self-report risky, even if she had first access.\n\nI don\u2019t think we have enough certainty to vote someone out here. I\u2019m okay with skip, but next round I want people to pay close attention to Eve and me if you\u2019re worried, and we should try to stay paired so there\u2019s better info."}}
